# P17 on GtkBackend on macOS (TEST_BACKEND=gtk4): step the three sizing controls (picker #161, aspect ratio in a ScrollView #266a, ideal-width VStack #266b) and read the numbers they print.
# Measured 2026-10-16 from p17-macos-gtk4-final-20261016-013213.png (1800x1736, halved to 900x868; origin=frame, 28 pt native title bar, geometry frame=(510,75) client=(510,103)). The capture is the launch geometry: Shorter/Taller ended where they began.
# The AppKit file's Less height / More height clicks (y 736) landed in the coloured stack on GTK's taller layout; the buttons are at frame y 796-829 (gtk4-aim-20261016.csv2). The picker row, picker and Shorter/Taller had landed and are re-centred.
# Derived, not measured: Shorter/Taller move by 5 pt per press and More height by up to 20 pt after Less height, so those rows aim where the button sits in every case (y 548 and y 802) rather than at the capture centre.
# After this file: presses: SML--++<> and stack: 145 x 140 again after one Less and one More.
# macOS 上 GtkBackend 的 P17:Less/More height 依 GTK 擷圖重新量測；按鈕會隨高度移動的列取各狀態共同可命中的 y。
